-- title:
--   Index of n-th powers in Kᵥ^× when μₙ ⊆ Kᵥ
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be a number field and let $v$ be a point of the height-one spectrum of its ring of integers $\mathcal{O}_K$, with $v$-adic completion $K_v$ and valuation ring $\mathcal{O}_v \subseteq K_v$. Let $n$ be a natural number and assume that the set of primitive $n$-th roots of unity in $K_v$ is nonempty, i.e. $K_v$ contains an element of exact order $n$ in the sense of `primitiveRoots`. Write $(K_v^\times)^n$ for the range of the $n$-th power endomorphism `powMonoidHom n` of the unit group $K_v^\times$, a subgroup since $K_v^\times$ is commutative. The assertion is the conjunction of two statements about the cardinality of the quotient group $K_v^\times / (K_v^\times)^n$, measured by `Nat.card`: first, that it equals $n^2$ times the cardinality of the quotient ring $\mathcal{O}_v / n\mathcal{O}_v$, where $n\mathcal{O}_v$ is the ideal generated by the image of $n$ in $\mathcal{O}_v$; and second, that this cardinality is nonzero, which, since `Nat.card` vanishes exactly on infinite types, says that the quotient $K_v^\times / (K_v^\times)^n$ is finite (and hence so is the right-hand side).
--
--   This is the local computation of the index $[K_v^\times : (K_v^\times)^n]$ at a finite place under the assumption $\mu_n \subseteq K_v$, obtained from the corresponding count $[\mathcal{O}_v^\times : (\mathcal{O}_v^\times)^n] = n \cdot \#(\mathcal{O}_v/n)$ for the unit group of the valuation ring together with the extra factor $n$ coming from the valuation $K_v^\times \to \mathbb{Z}$. It feeds the global product formula over all places of $K$ used in the Kummer-theoretic counting of $n$-th power classes.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_NumberField_natCard_units_adicCompletion_quotient_range_powMonoidHom.lean

